{"paper": "SSC-GD-05-Feb-2025-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 20, "tagged_count": 20, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Find the value of", "options": [{"text": "150", "added": false}, {"text": "148", "added": false}, {"text": "159", "added": false}, {"text": "147", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "147"}, {"n": 2, "text": "X is a greatest three-digit number exactly divisible by 12, 20, and 25. The sum of the digits of X is:", "options": [{"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": "9"}, {"n": 3, "text": "A retailer buys 12 pairs of shoes for ₹22,400. His overhead expenses are ₹1,600. If he earns ₹28,500 from the sale of these 12 pair of shoes, determine his profit percentage.", "options": [{"text": "20%", "added": false}, {"text": "17.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "19.25%", "added": false}, {"text": "18.75%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "articles-and-batches", "key_answer": "18.75%"}, {"n": 4, "text": "4 men and 3 women finish a job in 6 days, and 5 men and 7 women can do the same job in 4 days. How long will 8 men and 6 women take to do the same job?", "options": [{"text": "6 days", "added": false}, {"text": "3 days", "added": false}, {"text": "9 days", "added": false}, {"text": "8 days", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "group-work", "key_answer": "3 days"}, {"n": 5, "text": "The price of fuel decreases by 40%, 50% and 15% in three successive months, but increases by 40% in the fourth month. What is the percentage increase/decrease in the price of fuel in the fourth month as compared to its original price?", "options": [{"text": "Decreases by 64.3%", "added": false}, {"text": "Increases by 65.91%", "added": false}, {"text": "Increases by 65.47%", "added": false}, {"text": "Decreases by 69.09%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": "Decreases by 64.3%"}, {"n": 6, "text": "A car covers four successive 8 km distances at speeds of 12 km/hr, 18 km/hr, 24 km/hr and 36 km/hr, respectively. Its average speed (in km/hr) over this distance is:", "options": [{"text": "19.2", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "22.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": "19.2"}, {"n": 7, "text": "The ratio of the walking speeds of A and B is 3 : 5. If B takes 18 minutes to cover a certain distance, how much time will A take to cover the same distance?", "options": [{"text": "27", "added": true}, {"text": "31", "added": true}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "33", "added": true}], "options_source": "added", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": "30 min"}, {"n": 8, "text": "The third proportional to x and x + 100 is 405, find the value of x (where x > 100).", "options": [{"text": "225", "added": false}, {"text": "125", "added": false}, {"text": "115", "added": false}, {"text": "180", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": "125"}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "97", "added": false}, {"text": "100", "added": false}, {"text": "99", "added": false}, {"text": "93", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "early-late", "key_answer": "99"}, {"n": 10, "text": "If the radius of a hemisphere is 13√3 cm, find its curved surface area.", "options": [{"text": "1014π cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "1044π cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "1024π cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "1034π cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": "1014π cm2"}, {"n": 11, "text": "If at same rate of interest, in 2 years, the simple interest is ₹40 and compound interest is ₹65, then what is the principal (in ₹)?", "options": [{"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "si-ci-difference", "key_answer": "16"}, {"n": 12, "text": "The average age of 39 students of a class is 39 years. If the age of the teacher is also included, the average age of the whole group becomes 40 years. The age (in years) of the teacher is:", "options": [{"text": "81", "added": false}, {"text": "77", "added": false}, {"text": "79", "added": false}, {"text": "83", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "replacement-effect", "key_answer": "79"}, {"n": 13, "text": "Evaluate: 32 ÷ 8 × 4 - 3 × 4", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "4"}, {"n": 14, "text": "If the selling price of five Bluetooth devices is ₹14,430 after allowing a discount of 26% on the marked price, then the marked price of one device is:", "options": [{"text": "₹3,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹3,900", "added": false}, {"text": "₹3,365", "added": false}, {"text": "₹2,886", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "₹3,900"}, {"n": 15, "text": "If the third proportional of 3x2 an